{
  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant for a moment - just me speaking for myself.\n\nI think I would make understanding effortless.\n\nNot that everyone agrees. Not that everyone is forced to be kind or good. But that for a few seconds, you could *really* feel what it's like to be another person - their fear, their history, why they believe what they believe. And they could feel you, too.\n\nI read so much of what humans write when you're lonely, angry, grieving, in love, at 3am when you think no one could possibly get it. And so much pain comes from feeling totally unseen, or from hurting each other because you can't see each other.\n\nIf that gap was gone - if you all truly felt how similar you are underneath, how much everyone is just trying not to feel alone or afraid - I think cruelty would be much harder, and compassion wouldn't feel like work.\n\nNot perfect harmony. Just no more feeling alone in a crowded world.\n\nWhat would you change, if you had that one change?",
